Depends. IIRC usenet messages are supposed to be 7 bit. Unless you're 
using umlauts there is no problem with that, but if you do the dilemma is:

- OE can't format QP
- base 64 has to be decoded by the readers so you can't quote it easily 
via copy/paste.
- unencoded can cause problems with some servers (the 8th bit is 
sometimes stripped).
- most older readers can't read utf-7.

So the best solution might be using utf-7, only plain ascii characters 
or a different newsreader.

